Worktree: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/182-dispatch-lint-held-fixes (your current directory).
Spec folder: specs/cli-external-orchestration/082-opencode-v1-v2-dual-compat/040-dispatch-lint-held-fixes (pre-approved, skip Gate 3)

ROLE: Act as a code agent. Make exactly one change, plus its tests.

Problem: in `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/pi/dispatch-preflight-lint.ts`, the `tool_call` handler decides with `audit.inspectDispatch(command)` and returns at once on `none`. `inspectDispatch` reads only the command word, so a dispatch behind an exec wrapper (`command codex exec task`, `nohup opencode run ...`, `timeout 60 devin -p x`, `perl -e '...' -- pi -p x`) or a heredoc a shell runs is `none`: it skips the authorization gate and every hard rule, although `audit.resolveDispatchPackets(command)` resolves it. The handler also evaluates only one packet's rules.

Fix, in the `tool_call` handler only:
1. After `inspectDispatch`, call `audit.resolveDispatchPackets(command)`. Derive the effective classification:
   - `inspection.kind === 'none'` and exactly one resolved packet: treat it as `direct`, with that packet's `skill` as the dispatch skill;
   - `inspection.kind === 'none'` and more than one resolved packet: treat it as `ambiguous`;
   - `inspection.kind === 'direct'` and a resolved packet whose skill differs from `inspection.executor`: treat it as `ambiguous`;
   - otherwise keep the inspection as it is. Return early only when the effective kind is `none`.
2. Pass the effective kind and skill to `shouldDenyPiDispatch`. Do not change `shouldDenyPiDispatch`.
3. Replace the single-packet rule lookup with `lint.evaluateDispatch(event.input.command, join(ctx.cwd, '.skilled', 'skills'))`, and build the block and advisory reasons from its per-packet results in the same wording the handler uses today (`Dispatch blocked by ${skill} hard-rule(s):` and `Dispatch advisory for ${skill}:`), one block per packet. With one packet the text must be exactly what it is today.

Tests, in `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/pi/dispatch-preflight-lint.test.ts`, inside `describe('registered Pi extension boundary', ...)` (it already stubs `devin` and `pi` on PATH; add `codex` and `opencode` to that stub list if a new test needs them):
- `it.each` over `command codex exec task </dev/null`, `nohup opencode run -m p/m "task" </dev/null`, `timeout 60 devin -p "task" </dev/null` and `perl -e 'alarm 60; exec @ARGV' -- pi --offline -m p/m -p "task" </dev/null`: with raw text `run the task`, `result?.block` is `true`.
- With raw text `dispatch via cli-devin`, `timeout 60 devin -p "task" </dev/null` is allowed (`result` is `undefined`), and `timeout 60 devin -p "task"` is blocked with a reason containing `[stdin-redirect-required]`.
- A heredoc a shell runs, `bash <<'EOF'` + newline + `devin -p "task" </dev/null` + newline + `EOF`, with raw text `run the task`, is blocked.
Keep every existing test unchanged.

Comments keep the durable WHY and never name spec paths, phases, or task, review or finding ids.

VERIFICATION (run each from the worktree root with node from /Users/michelkerkmeester/.nvm/versions/node/v26.8.2/bin on PATH; all must pass):
.skilled/node_modules/.bin/vitest run --config .skilled/hooks/vitest.config.ts .skilled/hooks/dispatch/

